<title>HUNGARY: HUNGARIAN MAN KILLED BY BUS USED AT U.S. BASE.</title>
<headline>HUNGARIAN MAN KILLED BY BUS USED AT U.S. BASE.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>A 76-year-old Hungarian man was killed by a bus used by a defence subcontractor at the U.S. base in Hungary for Bosnian peacekeeping troops, the U.S. Army said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The victim was struck on Monday night near Dombovar, southwest Hungary, by one of three buses driving from Tuzla, Bosnia, to the U.S. support bases at Kaposvar and Taszar, an army statement said.</p>
<p>Hungarian police and the U.S. army's military police are investigating, the statement said.</p>
</text>
